{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/67922-wraith-questions","id":67922,"title":"Wraith questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-08T09:00:37-08:00","id":67922,"title":"Wraith questions","content":"Ok so a buddy of mine is relaunching his CWoD game and i am looking to play a wraith in it. What pdf/books will aid me and or the St in a game set in the realworld? Is it even possible for this character to be long term viable in such a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2228-darth-razmus","name":"Darth Razmus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T11:21:10-08:00","id":67986,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the easiest way to do it, especially for your ST, would be for you to play a Risen, that is a Wraith possessing his/her old corpse ala Crow, in which case you would need Wraith Core and Risen book.<br /> <br /> If not going the Risen route you will remain in the Shadowlands unless currently using either Puppetry or Embody which means that the ST just got another whole world to lay out for you. Still if not going with the Risen route then you would be advised to put all your arcanoi dots to either Embody, in which case the Wraith core is enough, or Puppetry, in which case you would benefit from having Guildbook Pardoners and Puppeteers as well.<br /> <br /> I should add that Shadow Players Guide is just too good to miss, but it isn't essential, and it's most of use to whomever plays your Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T11:32:02-08:00","id":67995,"title":"","content":"Is this a crossover game we're talking about here or just a WtO game? If a crossover game I recommend against it especially with WtO. And what do you mean by 'realworld'? If you're referring to the Skinlands (the world of the living) than yes if they have Embody they can crossover into the Skinlands. But don't remember how long they can do so.<br /> <br /> However you may want to try Orpheus where the ghost can no longer pass through the Shroud and are now stuck in the Skinlands rather than the Underworld. It's also a bit easier to handle as the mechanics of Orpheus as it isn't as difficult as WtO. But they use the normal human stat line at character creation, Attributes at 6/4/3 instead of 7/5/3 and Abilities at 11/7/4 instead of 13/9/5, instead of the supernatural stat line. Of course if this is a crossover game you could raise up the starting values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T12:05:02-08:00","id":68007,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">IIRC, Embody 4 lets a Wraith cross over for one scene per success. I think they look all ghostly and ectoplasmically corspified, but it still lets them interact with everything in the Skinlands. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">If a crossover is your troupe\u2019s shtick, maybe you and the ST can come up with some nifty artifact/gadget/McGuffin that increases the duration of this power. <br /> <br /> Happy Haunting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}